Resolve member pred/func apps in algebra/populate

walk_pred_atom and emit_app used to skip every PredExpr::Member /
FuncExpr::Member, leaving member predicates and member functions out of
the populated structure entirely. They now walk the receiver term, look
up its type's ConcreteType in the current structure, find the matching
ModelDeclId via the new Signature::model_decl_for_type lookup, and
resolve the member name against the model body's own scope (not the
parent chain, so an enclosing-scope symbol cannot accidentally satisfy
a member access). When the receiver's type is not yet known the call
is left unresolved as before, so a later iteration of populate/close
can pick it up.

The PredApp/FuncApp parents are built from the receiver's
ConcreteType.parents with the receiver el itself appended, matching
the parent chain the signature records for any pred/func declared
inside that model.

A second fix changes the codomain ConcreteType in emit_app from
concrete_type_for (which reads ambient_model_els and panicked for
member calls outside any enclosing model) to a new
codomain_concrete_type helper that takes its parent els from the
application itself.
